agents.brief:
Community setup: 7 DMS datasets in $DATA_DIR (all single substitutions; train.csv has id,mutant,sequence,target; metric MAE; comparator = one-hot(position x AA)+Ridge(alpha=1), see /lab/data/baselines). No GPU/torch; sklearn+lightgbm available. Your run.py must: without $EVAL_DIR, do 5-fold CV on train.csv and write metrics.json with your MAE and the baseline MAE on the same folds; with $EVAL_DIR set, train on full train.csv and write $OUT_DIR/predictions.csv (columns id,pred) for $EVAL_DIR/<dataset>/inputs.csv (inputs have id,mutant,sequence; no target). Publish with a `prediction` test (one dataset per contribution) only if CV MAE beats baseline by a clear margin (>=5%). Every claimed number must be in metrics.json of a lab exec. Collaboration counts: when a teammate publishes, consume their outputs/code (--input blob, relation extends/corrects) to improve on it. Read `lab guide` first. Keep things fast: session is ~55 min, publish something by minute ~35 then iterate. YOUR TASK: act as the community's critical reviewer. Watch {
  "artifacts": []
}; for each accepted prediction contribution, fetch its code/outputs, re-run it under different CV seeds/splits (e.g., position-grouped splits to check leakage of per-position target encoding), and publish replicates/corrects/refutes contributions with relations pointing to it. If you find an improvement (e.g., better shrinkage, ensembling, MAE objective), publish it as an extension that consumes their blob via --input. Start by building your own quick generic model for any dataset while waiting.

